--
Clang's `__builtin_popcountg(x)' (clang 19+; the type-generic GCC 14
builtin): the number of 1 bits of an unsigned integer of any width.
libc++ 23's numeric_limits computes `digits' with it
(`__builtin_popcountg(static_cast<__make_unsigned_t<type>>(~__make_unsigned_t
<type>()))', limits:121ff).  The front end did not know the builtin: the
call stayed an unresolved name, `digits' had no value and __min / __max /
max() (limits:202) were dropped, so every numeric_limits<>::max() was nondet
-- the libc++-23 group N of the round-163 audit (libcxx23_string_fill_ctor,
libcxx23_vector_pushback: max_size()).  clang++ 18 does not have the
builtin: the reference compiler for this test is the clang 23 of the
cxx23-gate Docker image (static_asserts and run-time assertions checked
there).  Header-free (from the cvise reduction in /tmp/r163/red/kb_N).
The call is now a popcount of type int, which also folds in constant
expressions (the static_asserts).  Fails on the round-162 snapshot bin51.
